  "notes": "REGISTER: Very formal/humble ({謙譲語|けんじょうご}). Used in business and service contexts.\n\nTRANSITIVITY: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive). Pattern: Xを{承|うけたまわ}る.\n\nUSAGE: This is a humble verb used when the speaker receives something from someone of higher status.\n\nCOMMON IN:\n・Customer service (receiving orders, reservations)\n・Business settings (receiving instructions)\n・Formal correspondence\n\nNORMAL EQUIVALENTS:\n・{聞|き}く (to hear - neutral)\n・{受|う}ける (to receive - neutral)\n・{伺|うかが}う (to hear/ask - humble but less formal)\n\nNOTE: Often appears as {承|うけたまわ}りました (received) in service industry.",
